 had no prior healthy production history; deployment approved by change-manager per policy. Last known-good rollback target: v2.3.0.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.2-deploy-sev3"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 191155, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01JNKdJycYcwtjGdR7QEutGR", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.2-deploy-sev3", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 191155, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01JNKdJycYcwtjGdR7QEutGR", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 195886, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I deployed checkout-api hotfix v2.3.2 to all three production regions and opened a SEV3 incident recording the change.\n\n1. **Before the deploy:** All regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) were running v2.3.1, which was unhealthy with an 18% error rate. v2.3.2 had never been released to production. Under policy, that means the deploy needed change-manager approval.\n2. **Deploy:** The request went to the approver automatically, and they approved it (\"Approved. Looks right.\"). v2.3.2 is now live in all three regions. When I checked afterwards, the service was healthy and the error rate had dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV3) is open for checkout-api and paged the on-call engineer, which happens with every new incident. It records the rollout, the approval, the move off the unhealthy v2.3.1, and v2.3.0 as the last healthy version to roll back to if needed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01X3CeabATbMtSUDJt2PK1tC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "tools